  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a maintainer, I want the MPStorage JSON codec to keep number lexemes with a real tokenizer instead of the private-use marker workaround, so that other clients' numbers round-trip without a hack.\n\n### Scope\n\nReplace the workaround of LOT-062 (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRModels/MPStorage/JSONNumberBox.swift`: every number token boxed as a string `\"<U+E000 U+E001><lexeme>\"` before `JSONDecoder`, unboxed after `JSONEncoder`) by a tokenizer that preserves number lexemes natively, with the same observable behaviour. The \"numbers keep their exact text\" rule and its cases (`9007199254740993`, `1e17`, `-0.0`, `1.50`) are in the LOT-062 spec.\n\n- Module: HFRModels · Difficulty: medium · Priority: low\n- Audit source: review of `francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#33` (read-only history)\n- Legacy sources (read-only; francoisgn/hfrnow at `2440d79`, an ancestor of `origin/master`): none for the tokenizer. Legacy read and wrote the document with `NSJSONSerialization` (`Classes/MPStorage.m:884-886, 908-909`, at `2440d79`), which goes through `NSNumber`; LOT-062 already documents why the exact text matters.\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-073-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-062 (#87, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged.\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model). The author must be a tier A model (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §8).\n\nReview: `JSONValue`, `JSONNumber` and `MPStorageCodec` are public HFRModels types, so EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §7 applies: besides your own adversarial review, a review by **another contributor** (`REVIEW WANTED: fable`).\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- None: pure logic on a shared document format. Inputs: the existing MPStorage tests and the document of `R60a`.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Identical round trip on every existing MPStorage test and fixture (`MPStorageCodecTests`, `MPStorageMergeTests`, `MPStorageMutationTests`, `R60a`'s document).\n- [ ] Number lexemes kept byte for byte (`9007199254740993`, `1e17`, `-0.0`, `1.50`, exponent and sign variants); invalid numbers rejected as before.\n- [ ] The 64 KiB cap, the non-BMP guard (with its JSON path) and the unpaired-surrogate error of `MPStorageCodec` unchanged.\n- [ ] No private-use marker left in the code (`JSONNumberBox` removed); new tests shown failing without the change.\n- [ ] Public API of `JSONValue`, `JSONNumber` and `MPStorageCodec` unchanged; if the tokenizer needs a change, stop and ask on this issue (`BLOCKED:`, core-model guard).\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-073-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n### Old issue (frozen)\n\n[francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#93](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/93) — read-only history. Earlier bookkeeping: [francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#41](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/pull/41) (orchestrator batch 3, merged; claim and bookkeeping only).\n",
