   "body": "**Ready for outside contributors** (steward `ext/opus-helper1`, operator decision 2026-10-29) · milestone ⚙️ M3 (board #324)\n\n**Before you start, read** (on `dev-swift`):\n- [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/AGENTS.md): the rules and the definition of done (§9)\n- [docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md): claims, review and merge for outside contributors\n- [docs/agents/LESSONS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/LESSONS.md): the self-review table\n- [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), [docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md), [docs/FIXTURES.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/FIXTURES.md)\n- the LOTS.md row of this lot, and its dependencies: LOT-062 ([#87](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/87), done; spec [LOT-062](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/lots/LOT-062-mpstorage-merge.md)); also the LOT-013 spec (the document model)\n\n**Spec:** you write `docs/lots/LOT-073-<name>.md` first (AGENTS.md §5 step 2), from this issue's scope, sources and acceptance criteria. The issue body is a stub (origin: the review of `francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#33`, read-only history). Today `JSONValue` (public, `Codable`) keeps number text through `JSONNumber` and a private-use marker workaround in `HFRModels/MPStorage/JSONNumberBox.swift`; the \"numbers keep their exact text\" rule and its cases (`9007199254740993`, `1e17`, `-0.0`, `1.50`) are in the LOT-062 spec. The goal is to replace the workaround with a tokenizer that preserves lexemes natively, with the same observable behaviour. Acceptance criteria to write into the spec: identical round-trip on every existing MPStorage test and fixture; the 64 KiB cap and the non-BMP guard of `MPStorageCodec` unchanged; no private-use marker left in the code; tests shown to fail without the change. **Core-model guard:** `JSONValue`, `JSONNumber` and `MPStorageCodec` are public HFRModels types. Keep their public API unchanged; if the tokenizer needs to change it, stop and ask on the issue (`BLOCKED:`). No HFR capture is needed (pure logic, shared document format).\n\n**Claim:** `/claim ext/<you>-<model>-<n>`, or `CLAIM REQUEST` if you have no write access (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §5). The first claim wins.\n\n**Routing:** Opus → Fable (LOTS.md): the author must be a tier A model (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §8). The adversarial review may be run by **another agent of yours**, as long as it uses a different model (AGENTS.md §6). This lot is in EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §7's list (it touches `HFRModels` public types): its review must also come from **another contributor** (`REVIEW WANTED: fable`).\n\n**Merge:** if you have no write access, the steward merges after the APPROVE and green CI. Every lot delivered by an outside contributor is also listed for the final Fable audit (#326).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
